>That would seem like adding limitations for no reason (to those used
>to the game as it is). Why not raise monster AC and to-hit modifiers?

Because there's no real reason to do so. Nethack follows rules when it
comes to monster design, but once the player comes into the picture
all that is thrown out. The monsters all have AC's between 10 and -10,
and considerably more are above 5 than below 0.

The other reason for focusing it on the player is because the player
is really alone in the game, there's nothing in the game like the
player, and the player is the only thing breaking the rules. If you
make other things break rules, it may have an impact that can't be
immediately seen which doesn't necessasrily seem like a good idea to
me. 

That said I'm not proposing players not be allowed to break the -10 AC
limit, I'm suggesting something at least twice that so a player still
feels like a hero at the end of the game, he just doesn't feel like a
god. 

